<!DOCTYPE page SYSTEM "entities.dtd" >
<xpage:page xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xpage="http://eprints.org/ep3/xpage" xmlns:epc="http://eprints.org/ep3/control">
<xpage:title>Policies</xpage:title>
<xpage:body>

<div>

<p><epc:phrase ref="archive_name" /> is a curated catalogue of construction management research. It is not an open-access repository: it holds bibliographic records rather than full texts, and material is selected by the editor rather than deposited at will. The policies that apply to open-access repositories, and the registration schemes that describe them are, therefore, not applicable here.</p>

<p>What governs this catalogue is set out on the pages below.</p>

<ul>
  <li><a href="/info_choosing_papers.html">Choosing papers</a> — how journals are selected, by cross-citation analysis rather than reputation, and how doctoral theses are identified.</li>
  <li><a href="/info_research_quality.html">Research quality</a> — why the catalogue records what the field has produced rather than judging which of it is worth reading.</li>
  <li><a href="/context.html">About <epc:phrase ref="archive_name" /></a> — the background to the field and why the catalogue is scoped as it is.</li>
  <li><a href="/information.html">Information</a> — general description of the service.</li>
</ul>

<p>Records are checked before they appear. Contributors with an account may deposit, but nothing enters the catalogue until it has been reviewed and approved by the editor.</p>

<p>Corrections are welcome. If you find an error in a record, or think a journal should be added to or removed from the catalogue, please get in touch using the details below.</p>

</div>
